This project is derived from the multi-index-lru library, which is part of
the userver framework (https://github.com/userver-framework/userver).

The ExpirableContainer functionality was originally derived from the expirable
branch at https://github.com/hzhdlrp/userver/tree/expirable/libraries/multi-index-lru
and has since been synchronized with the implementation in userver develop.

The original work is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Modifications from the original:
- Removed userver framework dependencies (USERVER_NAMESPACE macros, etc.)
- Adapted to be a standalone header-only library
- Added C++20 features ([[nodiscard]], noexcept, auto parameters)
- Added iteration support and explicit safe/unsafe underlying-container accessors
- Created standalone CMake build system
- Added ExpirableContainer with TTL-based expiration
- Added zerialize integration for serialized binary data caching
- Added owning-byte SBE/sbepp integration
- Added reusable extracted-node pooling and an injectable expiration clock
